    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nTaxonomy of Step-by-Step Reasoning\nErrors\nROSCOE: A SUITE OF METRICS FOR SCORING STEP-BYSTEP REASONING",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 136
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 127,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nReasoning Scorer: ROSCOE\n•\nSuite of metrics for scoring Step-by-Step reasoning\n•\nSource context of T sentences indicating a problem statement followed by a\nquestion and is prompted to generate step-by-step reasoning\n•\nHypothesis of N-steps, including a final answer as the last step\n•\nGold step-by-step reasoning of K steps (may or may not be available)\nROSCOE: A SUITE OF METRICS FOR SCORING STEP-BYSTEP REASONING",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 448
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 128,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nReasoning Scorer: ROSCOE\n•\nFine-grained metrics under 4 categories\n1.\nSemantic-Alignment Metrics\n2.\nSemantic-Similarity Metrics\n3.\nLocal Inference Metrics\n4.\nLanguage Coherence Metrics\nROSCOE: A SUITE OF METRICS FOR SCORING STEP-BYSTEP REASONING",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 279
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 129,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nReasoning Alignment Vector\n•\nReasoning alignment vector from the N-step hypothesis h to the source\ns of length T\nnormalized cosine similarity between hypothesis step and most similar sentence in a context\n•\nMeasures the grounding of the step-wise reasoning with respect to the\nsource text",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 322
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 130,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nSemantic Alignment Metrics",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 60
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 131,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nSemantic Similarity Metrics\n•\nQuantify the degree of semantic equivalence between pieces of text\n•\nConsiders text as a whole, rather than relying on text units comparisons",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 205
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 132,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nLogical Inference Metrics\n•\nMeasure logical errors between pieces of text\n•\nUse a Natural Language Inference (NLI) model trained to classify\nhypothesis-context pairs into entailment, neutral, and contradiction\nclasses to infer the contradiction probability",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 290
  },
  {
    "source": "lecture_05.pdf",
    "page": 133,
    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nLanguage Coherence Metrics\n•\nUse perplexity PPL as scored by the GPT2-Large model and English\ngrammatical acceptability p_gram scores",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 167
