    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nTravelPlanner\nAre language agents capable of planning in more complex yet realistic settings,\ncloser to those in which humans operate?\n•\nTravel planning is a challenging, time-consuming task\n•\n1,225 user queries along with their reference plans\nFindings\n•\nState-of-the-art LLMs cannot handle complex planning tasks like those in\nTravelPlanner. GPT-4 successfully produces a plan that meets all the constraints\nfor a few tasks (0.6%)\n•\nPlanning strategies such as ReAct and Reflexion are insufficient for the multi-\nconstraint tasks\n•\nCommon failure modes of existing language agents, such as argument errors in\ntool use, being trapped in dead loops, and hallucinations\nTravelPlanner: A Benchmark for Real-World Planning with Language Agents",
    "method": "native",
    "native_text_length": 774
